#pragma once
#include "game/Quests.h"
#include <array>
namespace rpg {
inline constexpr std::array<QuestDefinition,frontierQuestCount> frontierQuests{{
 {"The broken watch","Beacon Keeper","Defeat the three watch deserters north of Dawnwatch.","The anchor is quiet, but our watch has splintered. Three deserters have taken the northern patrol ground. Drive them away before the evening supply caravan arrives.","The deserters still hold the northern patrol ground. Defeat all three, then return to me.","The road is ours again. Your report will help rebuild the watch.","Your service has been recorded. The next dispatch is ready.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"Ash on the road","Beacon Keeper","Defeat the three ash marauders on the northern patrol ground.","Tracks in the ash belong to a second warband. Their heavy fighter leads two scouts. Break the group before they find the village stores.","The ash marauders are still abroad. Their captain hits hard; watch the wind-up.","The stores are safe. Take this field experience into your next battle.","The marauder report is complete.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"Voices beyond the beacon","Beacon Keeper","Defeat three veilbound intruders north of the outpost.","Last night the beacon answered voices that were not ours. Veilbound intruders now stalk the old patrol route. Silence them before they reach the anchor.","Three intruders must fall. Keep a clear path back to the village.","The voices have stopped. We can hear our own signals again.","The veilbound incursion is contained.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"The iron tribute","Beacon Keeper","Defeat the three iron collectors on the northern patrol ground.","A captain demands tribute in iron and grain. His collectors have occupied our patrol road. Dawnwatch will not pay with its winter stores.","The collectors carry heavy protection. Use your class disciplines and recover between engagements.","You have bought the village another winter. The council recognises your service.","The tribute demand has been refused.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"A lantern in the mist","Beacon Keeper","Defeat three mist hunters north of Dawnwatch.","The night patrol followed a false lantern. Mist hunters now wait along their route. Clear the ground so our missing sentries can return safely.","The hunters are still waiting beyond the outpost. Defeat all three.","Our sentries have found their way home. Your report belongs in the watch archive.","The false lantern is extinguished.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"The last oath","Beacon Keeper","Defeat the three oathbreakers on the northern patrol ground.","The enemy has sent its sworn guard. Their oath is to take our beacon. Hold the northern approach and prove that our own oath is stronger.","The oathbreakers will not retreat. Defeat their entire squad.","The beacon still burns. Few recruits could have held that ground.","Your oath has been honoured.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"Keeper of the frontier","Beacon Keeper","Defeat the three siege champions north of Dawnwatch.","This is their final assault: three siege champions, each carrying the strength of the defeated warbands. Meet them on the northern patrol ground. Return alive, and Dawnwatch will remember your name.","The final champions remain. Prepare your build and keep your recovery ready.","The frontier is secure. You have earned the standing of a veteran of Dawnwatch.","Dawnwatch is safe. Warden Elian awaits beyond the western dock; follow the west road to his lodge.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"The west road opens","Warden Elian","Defeat three roadbreakers in Westward Reach, then report to Elian.","You have held a village. Now help us reach the people beyond it. Roadbreakers have cut the old west road between my lodge and the northern ridge. Their captain carries our missing watch seal. Clear the three positions; I will send word to the coast surveyor.","Follow the dirt road north from my lodge. Three roadbreakers remain between us and the ridge; their retreat paths lead back to their camps.","The west road is open again. Our messengers can travel without an armed escort. Mara is waiting at the eastern survey house.","Take the road east through the training grounds. Surveyor Mara needs eyes and a steady hand more than another sword.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"An honest map","Surveyor Mara","Inspect the three coastal survey stones with E, then return to Mara.","Our oldest map puts a safe path where the cliffs have broken away. I have marked three survey stones: the low coast, the far headland and the northern overlook. Visit each, read its bearing and return. Do not trust a straight line across an unknown shore.","Three bearings make a trustworthy survey. The atlas marks the nearest unread stone. Stand beside it and press E; your notes will survive the journey home.","These bearings agree. There is still a route to the bastion. Serevan can now guide a company there without sending it over the edge.","Bring this knowledge north. Archivist Serevan waits at the shelter beyond the old anchor, beside the road to the bastion.",0,250,Item::None,false},
 {"The bastion remembers","Archivist Serevan","Defeat three bastion sentinels in the far north, then return to Serevan.","Before Dawnwatch, there was a bastion. Its last sentinels still obey a signal whose keepers are long dead. Mara has found the road; Elian has secured our retreat. Break the three sentinels' watch so we may recover the names of those who built this place.","The sentinels hold the northern court. Their heavy blows can be read and interrupted. Keep the return road behind you, and do not let their captain corner you against the ruin.","The court is silent. We can recover its records without adding another name to the dead. You have joined three isolated outposts into one frontier.","The twelve assignments are complete. Dawnwatch, the western lodge and the coast are connected again. The training post remains open.",0,250,Item::None,false}
}};
}
